    "project_description": "Enviro Rise is an initiative developed in the PT Rimbun Seruyan concession, which spans 34,250 hectares across the Seruyan and Kotawaringin Timur Regencies. With 62% of the area consisting of degraded peatlands, our mission is to transition from an industrial forest plantation business model which involves forest clearing and peatland drainage to one focused on actively restoring and conserving these vital ecosystems. The project also prioritizes the protection of critically endangered species, such as the Bornean orangutan (Pongo pygmaeus). In parallel, we work to empower local communities by promoting sustainable livelihood opportunities and supporting access to higher education.",
